{"id": "unknown-2026-10-10-005", "date": "2026-10-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Germany lifts 2026 growth forecast to 1.3%", "content": "Germany raised its 2026 economic growth forecast to 1.3 per cent from 0.5 per cent and lifted its 2027 outlook to 1.1 per cent, according to the Ministry of Economy and Energy. \nExports, public spending and investment are expected to support recovery despite risks from the Middle East and Ukraine. \nInflation is forecast at 2.7 per cent in 2026 and 3.0 per cent in 2027. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/germany-lifts-2026-growth-forecast-to-1-3--314139-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-10-006", "date": "2026-10-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["fast_fashion"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Britain’s unworn clothes waste billions of litres of water: Oxfam", "content": "An Oxfam UK report has claimed that social media is fuelling fast fashion, placing digital influence in focus for the apparel and fashion sector. \nIt found that 32 per cent of the average UK wardrobe has not been worn in the past year, while four in 10 people have worn an item of clothing just once. \nThe water used to produce those barely worn garments would fill about 88 billion single-use water bottles.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/britain-s-unworn-clothes-waste-billions-of-litres-of-water-oxfam-314048-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
